      "prompt": "I would like to work on feedback from a cold-start agent and fix the gaps. the following feedback came from a cold-start agent that 1) did not run wake again after I gave it the project name (it wouldve been able to deduce from the directory we were in), and 2) instead of running it again, it went directly into the files and started digging around instead of using the tools- i told it not to do that again: Feedback from a real session (2026-11-08), agent = Ori intern (z-ai/glm-5.3-flash) on\nproject ai-flutter-chat, using the mnemos MCP server.\n\nOBSERVED: The agent fell back to filesystem reads of the vault when retrieval\ndisappointed, and the tool contract didn't prevent it.\n\n1. CONTRACT GAP — MCP-only access rule is not stated anywhere.\n   A cold agent with only the ten tool descriptions fell back to filesystem reads\n   (`ls`, `find`, `read`) of ~/ori-memory-vault/** when ranked queries disappointed.\n   Fix: add one line to the wake response (and/or mnemos://manual):\n\n   \"Vault access is MCP-only: never read or write vault files (~/ori-memory-vault/**)\n   via shell or file tools. All access goes through the mnemos tools; if a capability\n   is missing, ask the user rather than bypassing the server.\"\n\n   Also consider a `vault-access=mcp-only` token in the policy summary line\n   (`purge=approval · identity=approval · ...`).\n\n2. TWO-STEP WAKE IS DESIGNED BUT NOT ENFORCED.\n   The agent skipped the project-scoped wake (wake with project=<tag>) after the user\n   answered the project question, and instead ran three fuzzy query_ranked calls plus\n   a direct file read. Fix: when `project_choice_required` is present, either\n   (a) fail fast on queries — \"session not booted for project X; call wake with\n   project=<tag>\" — or (b) make the wake response carry a stronger, harder-to-ignore\n   instruction that the agent must re-call wake with the project tag.\n\n3. RANKED QUERIES RETURN TITLES-WITHOUT-CONTENT.\n   The agent had to switch to `explore` (which returns snippets) or read files.\n   Fix: include a short content excerpt in ranked results, or merge the explore\n   behavior into ranked retrieval.\n\n4. WARMTH RERANKING DEMOTED THE MAP NOTE.\n   ai-flutter-chat-map was demoted #1 → #6 on its own most relevant query. A MOC/map\n   note should probably rank high regardless of warmth. Fix: protect hub/MOC notes\n   from warmth demotion.\n\n5. COMMIT HASH DISCREPANCY IN MAP VS GOALS.\n   Map file says eb4874; goals say eb74874. Worth fixing in the map next time it's\n   touched.\n\n6. PROVENANCE / CONFABULATION GUARD.\n   The agent generated a confident caveat (\"my earlier hand-labeled feedback came from\n   a different instance — the source map is worth a refresh\") that was actually\n   confabulated — the agent had no record supporting it. Fix: mnemos should distinguish\n   observed/witnessed facts from agent-issued advisories at the storage layer, and if\n   agent-issued advisories persist across contexts, they should be clearly labeled.\n   Also: give the agent a way to check its own prior feedback via MCP (\"what feedback\n   did I give before?\" — a refreshable source map), rather than requiring the agent to\n   confabulate from adjacent warmth.\nItems 1–4 are the ones that directly caused the behavior you're trying to fix; 5 is a small data hygiene fix; 6 is the design guard that would have caught the caveat before it reached you.",
